From: Project SunUEFI <sunuefi@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: add ordinary IGC v5 through shared REGDMA color state

Expose the verified ordinary 257-entry, 16-bit IGC v5 layout through standard
DEGAMMA_LUT. Use R/G/B LUTBUS transfers, the published three-NOP workaround,
and IGC control enable at DSPP 0x1264. Preserve the standard endpoint including
zero; leave high precision and dither disabled.

Merge complete GC and IGC state in the existing REGDMA BO and queue. Calculate
the final descriptor offset from the actual command length and reject an
out-of-buffer layout before taking clocks or publishing DMA. Existing GEM/VM,
mutex, PM/module/clock lifetime and unknown-queue reset retention are unchanged.

Keep assigned DSPPs for this backend even when both LUTs are bypassed, clear
unassigned duplicate pointers, and validate every actual split-display half.
On color change or modeset, submit both current LUTs (NULL disables each).
Only successful combined DMA stages GC/IGC flush; failure cannot apply PCC
alone. Other platforms keep their existing GC programming implementation.

Based on Piano source 95b72a5bd7eb7fb31b2b385faa915edeee5a31cf, tree
70a83a85970d3c6b50afe8886b4f6b855bd32d6a. Register/command ABI from MiCode
vendor_opensource_display-drivers aa06fd1757c28dce96fbe4e04d4530ec21b52aac.
This candidate is not in the default series. Seven ARM64 objects and actual
CPU packer boundary calls passed; no full kernel link or hardware test.
It does not implement high-precision sampling, HDR metadata or 12-bit FRC.
